# Show, don’t tell

Keep in sync with Place et Marque `preferences.md` (show-don’t-tell bullet).

## Ban (user-facing UI copy)

Do not paper over unclear UX with coaching such as:

- “Open X first…”
- “More options appear when…”
- “Click here to reveal…”
- Step-by-step GUI how-tos that exist only because the control is hidden or unlabeled

If the interaction is unclear, **fix the GUI**.

## Allowed

- Field helpers that explain what a **value** means (e.g. Product URL / “name in the link”).
- Domain/glossary affordances (e.g. TermHint) that are not progressive-disclosure coaching.

## Enforcement

- Agents: apply on every UX change and audit.
- Static phrase gate: `ops/tooling/prefs-lint/show-dont-tell-static.check.sh` (high-confidence patterns).
- AST/UI layout rules (icons, alignment, cart chrome) stay with ESLint `portfolio-prefs/*` (Angle B) — do not duplicate those here.
